  "caption": "Quinn's knees were grumbling on every footpath and staircase, so Kay suggested something unexpected: the pool.\n\nWater exercise is genuine rehab. Buoyancy takes some of the load off sore joints, so they can often move earlier and more comfortably, while the water gives gentle resistance in every direction.\n\nWhat often helps: walking, marching and squatting in waist-to-chest water (no swimming needed), using warm water for stiff joints, checking timing with your treating team after an injury or surgery, and then building up to land-based strength, which water alone doesn't fully provide.\n\nOpen wounds or some heart or skin conditions? Check with your GP before getting in.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
